   why_it_matters="With T in eV and n_e in cm^-3 the existing gate always fails (c ≈ 1e18), so the 2-D certificate is unit-dependent and in practice unusable. The invariant form is necessary and sufficient for the linearized Lipschitz matrix. It gives the coupled Aguilera–Aragón T–n_e loop (R9-02 Picard, R9-03 Anderson) a runtime check that does not depend on units.",
   pipeline_link="G2 TS-09 / frontiers/12 C11 (2-D jointOuterMap_contraction named as the analogous glue); R9-02/R9-03 (T–n_e fixed point, damping), R2-01(C)",
   literature="Elementary linear algebra (2×2 Perron–Frobenius / M-matrix criterion); no domain citation needed.",
   mathlib_prereqs="ContractingWith.exists_fixedPoint' (Topology/MetricSpace/Contracting.lean:152), Prod.dist_eq, isClosed_Icc.prod; the weight existence is nlinarith/polyrith algebra (choose wn/wT = (1−a)/b adjusted, or the Perron vector)",
   repo_anchors="SahaEquilibrium.lean:jointOuterMap, jointOuterMap_contraction (:1426), jointOuterContraction_box (:1585), outerContraction_box (1-D, already unit-invariant)",
   already_exists_check="rg -i 'spectral.radius|weighted max|weighted.*metric|rescal' CflibsFormal/ docs/frontiers/04-outer-t-iteration.md: no joint-map hits (only unrelated EquivalentWidth/Classic rescaling identities).",
